        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Echoes of Syntax</strong> is a retro-flavored arena roguelike where your magic comes from words.<br>Combine <strong>Nouns</strong> (projectile), <strong>Verbs</strong> (behavior), and <strong>Adjectives</strong> (element/effect) to create hundreds of spell variants — from <i>Fiery Chasing Orbs</i> to <i>Icy Bouncing Mines</i>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Word-crafting spells: mix <strong>Noun + Verb + Adjective</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fast wave-based combat with endless combos</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One new <strong>card unlock</strong> after each wave</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Simple, readable three-column word picker</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pixel-inspired UI, chiptune vibes, smooth camera</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Boss music &amp; a calm main menu theme</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Progression</strong><br>Start with a small deck of words, unlock a new one after each wave, and swap your build before diving back in. Find broken synergies and push for higher waves.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>(All screenshots show gameplay. Systems and content may evolve during development.)</i></p>",
